<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Amalric I of Jerusalem</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1136–<a href="/years/1174">1174</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Also known as Amalric of Jerusalem</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Amalric I was king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a> from 1163 to 1174. Before his accession he held the County of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jaffa">Jaffa</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ashkelon">Ascalon</a>. As king he led repeated invasions of Fatimid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> in the 1160s, competing with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nur-al-din">Nur al-Din</a>'s forces under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shirkuh">Shirkuh</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saladin">Saladin</a>, who ended up controlling Egypt. He was succeeded by his son Baldwin IV.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/amalric-i-of-jerusalem.jpg" alt="Amalric I of Jerusalem" width="320" height="510" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Amalric_receives_a_message_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The kingdom won important victories, including King Baldwin IV’s defeat of Saladin at the Battle of Montgisard in 1177, and King <b>Amalric</b> I invaded Egypt several times between 1163 and 1169, briefly forcing it to pay tribute.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-jerusalem">Kingdom of Jerusalem · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>From 1163 Nur ad-Din contested Egypt with <b>Amalric of Jerusalem</b>: Shirkuh, with his nephew Saladin, won the Battle of al-Babein in 1167, relieved Cairo in 1168 and in 1169 killed the vizier Shawar and seized Egypt for Nur ad-Din.</blockquote><a href="/empire/zengid-dynasty">Zengid dynasty · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>Baldwin III captured Ascalon from the Fatimids in 1153, and the combined county was given to his brother <b>Amalric</b>.</blockquote><a href="/state/county-of-jaffa-and-ascalon">County of Jaffa and Ascalon</a></li></ul></section>
